  <div class="text-primary-light text-shadow md:text-lg">
    I am a Data Analyst with three years of experience turning chaotic, fragmented data into clear, actionable intelligence. 
    I specialize in delivering real-time insights that help teams make confident decisions under pressure — whether stabilizing ad spend, managing risk, or pivoting workflows quickly in uncertain conditions. 
    What makes my work effective is the ability to combine technical rigor with a genuine understanding of how people actually use information. 
    That instinct for turning data into something that drives real movement is what shapes how I work.
    <br />
    <br />
    That same instinct for turning noise into clear action actually started in direct sales and property management. 
    That’s where I developed my skills in building rapport, managing messy logistics, and influencing outcomes when the stakes were high. 
    I initially jumped into tech through frontend development, but quickly realized I wanted to work directly with the data itself. 
    I wanted to find the hidden insights, spot trends, and turn raw numbers into stories that actually drive business decisions. 
    So I moved into data analysis and started engineering ETL pipelines to create that clarity at scale. 
    Earning my Google Project Management Certificate and PSM I gave me the exact structure I need to bring those insights to teams. 
    At the end of the day, the best data only matters when it helps real people move faster and smarter together.
    <br />
    <br />
    Outside of work, I bring the same intentionality to my life that I apply to data. 
    I stay grounded through daily calisthenics, clear my head by traveling, and channel my creativity into cooking, leatherworking, and mixing house music. 
    My most important ongoing project is building a house for my retired parents in Queretaro, and I also spend my time fostering dogs and helping them find new homes.
